(carried over) = 6.\nWrite down 6.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n    61739.\n  1.\n```.\n\n**Step 7: Add the digits in the millions place**.\n6 (from 666537775) + 3 (from 338039615) = 9.\nWrite down 9.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n  961739.\n  1.\n```.\n\n**Step 8: Add the digits in the ten-millions place**.\n6 (from 666537775) + 3 (from 338039615) = 9.\nWrite down 9.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n 9961739.\n  1.\n```.\n\n**Step 9: Add the digits in the hundred-millions place**.\n6 (from 666537775) + 3 (from 338039615) = 9.\nWrite down 9.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n99961739.\n  1.\n```.\n\n**Step 10: Add the digits in the billion place**.\n9 (from 666537775) + 3 (from 338039615) = 12.\nWrite down 2 and carry over 1.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n129961739.\n  1.\n```.\n\n**Step 11: Add the digits in the ten-billion place**.\n9 (from 666537775) + 3 (from 338039615) = 12.\nWrite down 2 and carry over 1.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n129961739.\n  1.\n```.\n\n**Step 12: Add the digits in the hundred-billion place**.\n1 (from 666537775) + 3 (from 338039615) = 4.\nWrite down 4.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n129961739.\n  1.\n```.\n\n**Step 13: Add the digits in the trillion place**.\n1 (from 666537775) + 3 (from 338039615) = 4.\nWrite down 4.\n\n```.\n  666537775.\n+ 338039615.\n-----------.\n129961739.\n  1.\n```. Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
